              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU POINT: the rare **ఙ** you met in **వాఙ్మయం**, once]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now imagine the cool patch beneath a tree. This lesson gives that patch a name, using the familiar య at the end and a different uncommon letter at the beginning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఛాయ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఛాయ — chāya — \"shade\" or \"shadow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it in two gentle pieces: chā, ya. The first sound is an airy ch; the second is the familiar య sound. Read the word as ఛా-య."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఛాయ (chāya) is a learned word with a wider range than one dark shape. In literary or careful language it can also name a reflected image or a tinge of colour. Keep the first meaning small today: shade or shadow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A useful image comes before an unfamiliar letter. You can say the whole word before the next lesson asks your hand to take its first shape apart."
            }
          ]
        },
